WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.330
A distinctive laterally traceable rock unit can be called a formation.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.430
A formation may contain many individual beds.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.270
Bedding can be defined by grain size, composition or color, and

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:13.450
the boundary between rock units is a contact.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.530
Contacts may be sharp, gradational or scoured;

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.690
a sharp boundary alone does not establish its cause.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.090
Layers can record a discrete flood, changes in current strength or

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.330
direction, a new sediment supply, changing sea level or changing climate.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.930
Each explanation needs the actual evidence.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.850
Different colors do not automatically mean different climates, and a thick

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:38.050
bed does not supply a universal amount of elapsed time.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.430
Shake mixed sediment in water and let it settle.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:45.730
Coarser particles settle first, with progressively finer material above.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:50.790
A normally graded bed therefore becomes finer upward as transport energy

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.310
wanes or suspended sediment settles.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.430
Read the variation within one bed.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.430
Water left above a jar deposit is not another sedimentary layer.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.350
A current moves grains over a dune or ripple crest.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:08.170
Grains accumulate on its down-current slope, and migrating dunes preserve inclined

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.890
layers called cross beds. Cross beds can form in water as

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:15.450
well as in wind. Large dune-scale sets and other clues support

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:19.330
a desert interpretation; inclined layers alone do not prove one.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.130
Parallel beds commonly form as layers accumulate on one another.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.550
A scoured contact instead records erosion before the next deposit.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.890
Keep parallel bedding, cross bedding and grading distinct:

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:36.750
they concern layer orientation, inclined internal deposits and an upward grain-size

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:40.990
change. Compare the actual source photograph before identifying the process.
